1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:04,100
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,221
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,740
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,917
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,420
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,677
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:16,800
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,897
We came to this new world
believing that surely someday.

11
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:37,977
We just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,297
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,237
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,017
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,200
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,820
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,637
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,617
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,157
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,897
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,680
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up, way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,637
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,160
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:47,460
listen white hunter i'm telling you
right now keep your distance from caesar.

54
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:51,957
last thing i need to deal with is us
taking turns squeezing each other's hearts.

55
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:54,637
i know you're filled
with hellfire right now

56
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:57,602
but save it until i get
my heart back from vergo.

57
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:02,860
as long as we're on this island
you're following my orders got it.

58
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,017
I took the shortest route here.

59
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:10,720
And I was moving as fast as I could.

60
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:15,440
Where are you? Vergo!

61
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,917
Damn it, you're incessantly irritating.

62
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,860
I got you.

63
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,940
Spoke too soon there.

64
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,160
Unflammable type.

65
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,980
Me, I'll gasp!

66
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:46,357
What's your problem?

67
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:48,497
What reason do you have for attacking me?

68
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:51,437
Other than you trying to kill me
and my friends and everyone else,

69
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:53,877
something cool's supposed
to happen if I capture you.

70
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:57,277
That sounds to me like you formed
some kind of alliance with Law.

71
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,257
Trusting him is an act of foolishness.

72
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,757
Take it from my own experience.

73
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,017
He will betray you.

74
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,100
Keep your advice!

75
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:05,780
I'll do whatever I wanna do!

76
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:09,266
You really are a glutton
for pain, aren't you?

77
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,110
Karakuni!

78
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,440
Oh, crap, I'm choking again.

79
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:20,525
Most people do that when
I remove their oxygen.

80
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,580
So this is the distance.

81
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:37,460
Yes, you've got me.

82
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,817
My powers are locked within a set radius.

83
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:43,312
The question is, how long can
you stay out of that radius?

84
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,700
Get ready for Gum-Gum!

85
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:49,340
I'm not giving you the jet!

86
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:51,900
Jet pistol!

87
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,600
That hurt, you dullard!

88
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:59,620
Although, it allowed me
to close the distance.

89
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,217
Not again.

90
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,620
That looks painful. Well, here.

91
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,194
Want your oxygen back?

92
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:10,120
Breathe in the blue sword.

93
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:17,020
Get ready to be slashed and seared.

94
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:23,220
Every gas is a weapon for me.

95
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,317
Maybe I can't kill you with poison,

96
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:29,177
but I've still got an entire arsenal
that'll put you in the ground.

97
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:31,613
I'm getting real tired of not breathing.

98
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:36,400
Quit running and give me your breath!

99
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:38,360
Quit chasing me!

100
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,000
Armament hardening!

101
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,840
This is it!

102
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:07,700
Gum-Gum, Jake Gottlieb!

103
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,360
Is that a wall?

104
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,120
Hey, what the hell? Igloo.

105
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:17,600
I'm impressed.

106
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:22,567
There aren't too many people alive that
could actually break through this wall.

107
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:26,900
You've got Devil Fruit powers?

108
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:30,277
It's time to go, Master.

109
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:35,717
this is a pointless fight you're
telling me so what you're just

110
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:40,357
gonna run do your worst Straw Hat
I've got bigger fish to fry but I'll

111
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:43,777
keep you in my thoughts when I use
your crew as test subjects for my

112
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:50,237
experiment enjoy your demise sorry

113
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:53,857
but you can't go after him I won't

114
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:58,817
let the master suffer any further
misfortune joker would kill me if

115
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:03,917
i allowed that you mean the pink
bird guy from the war what the hell

116
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,717
is up with that dude the gate's

117
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:11,337
closing we gotta run hooray ain't that

118
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:15,479
black-legged Sanji i don't get it
what's a Straw Hat doing helping us

119
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,780
Full power strike!

120
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,837
It don't look like Black
Lake's going to back down.

121
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,217
He's beating the hell
out of that fake Vergo.

122
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:35,817
We've got to give you some backup.

123
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:37,177
What are you morons doing?

124
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,554
Start running already.

125
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,779
They're trying to seal you
up in here to poison you.

126
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,459
What'd I tell you?

127
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,257
They're letting the gas in!

128
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:49,417
We better run for it!

129
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:50,380
Get a move on!

130
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:57,040
Well, look at that.

131
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,260
Now I get it.

132
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:03,093
You've got metal or something
under your skin, don't you?

133
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,000
Quit interfering.

134
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,640
This is an internal matter.

135
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:10,907
I'm familiar with your type.

136
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:13,020
My captain hates guys like you.

137
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,180
Oh, crap.

138
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,300
Hey, Blackley!

139
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:30,894
You're gonna run, man!

140
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,158
The main's closing!

141
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:34,457
You're gonna get trapped in there!

142
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:35,540
Turn around!

143
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,327
The gas is right behind you!

144
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,560
Get out of there!

145
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:45,160
This is an alert from Building D!

146
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:49,320
Attention all buildings in the
third laboratory! What now?

147
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:51,480
This is building D!

148
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,644
Attention all buildings
in the third laboratory!

149
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:58,400
The Warlord Shavulgar Law
has infiltrated the premises!

150
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:04,040
And he's just gained access
to the SAD Manufacturing Room!

151
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:08,380
Is he crazy?

152
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,896
What does that fool think he's doing?

153
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:16,760
If he goes through with this, he's gonna
bite off more than even he can chew!

154
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:22,680
So that's it.

155
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:25,180
That was his plan all along. What the?

156
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:29,440
You capture the Master
while he finds S .A .D.

157
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:32,860
Well, I finally see what
your little scheme is.

158
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:43,470
Law.

159
00:09:43,553 --> 00:09:46,967
He formed an alliance with the
Strawhats just to keep us busy.

160
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:51,571
And he probably joined the Warlords
just so he can gain access to that room.

161
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,480
Crazy bastard.

162
00:09:56,280 --> 00:10:00,880
He must have one seriously hellish
scenario banging around inside his skull.

163
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:06,500
Now, it's time to unleash
hell on the new world.

164
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:17,317
Whoa, hold on, don't close it yet.

165
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:20,157
Whoa, he's right, that fake
nirgle guy in Blackleg.

166
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,652
Haven't made it out yet.

167
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:23,977
It's too late.

168
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:26,557
The poison gas is about
to be all over the place.

169
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:27,837
There's nowhere to run.

170
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,057
They're dead.

171
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,300
Blackleg, no.

172
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,597
This isn't fair.

173
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,480
There's nothing we can do.

174
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:37,430
Hey.

175
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:39,897
Everyone made it.

176
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:42,020
You're looking good! It's him!

177
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,920
Especially you, sweetie!

178
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:45,520
You survived after all!

179
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:48,040
You really scared us, pal!

180
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,197
Keep on kicking ass, Blackwing!

181
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:51,257
Hey, you're awesome!

182
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:52,800
I don't care about you!

183
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,150
Gross!

184
00:10:54,233 --> 00:10:56,637
I don't need a bunch of ugly
dudes singing my praise.

185
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,550
Ladies only!

186
00:10:58,660 --> 00:10:59,700
Hey, you okay?

187
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:02,257
We can give you some
first aid if you got hurt.

188
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,170
Shut up!

189
00:11:03,253 --> 00:11:06,577
Unless you can get me a kiss from
your captain, then I don't care!

190
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:07,677
I got lucky.

191
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:09,940
That guy could have destroyed me.

192
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,840
Who was that bastard anyway?

193
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,017
Some commander of yours or something?

194
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:14,930
What?

195
00:11:15,013 --> 00:11:15,843
Not a chance!

196
00:11:15,926 --> 00:11:18,117
Yeah, that was just someone
pretending to be the Vice Admiral!

197
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,141
He's a good guy!

198
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:21,262
You tell him what's up, Captain!

199
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:25,200
No, it can't be him.

200
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:26,760
Vice Admiral Vergo.

201
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,417
He thinks of the G5 as a sort of family.

202
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,337
He'd never do something like that.

203
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:34,857
Well, I've never met the guy myself,
so I couldn't tell you either way.

204
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:37,677
I just know that he turned
pale and ran off somewhere.

205
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,957
At any rate, we should get moving soon.

206
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:44,057
We're going to save those children
and get everyone out of this place.

207
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:46,800
Hey, whatever you say, we're all on board!

208
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:50,960
Law's going after S .A .D.

209
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,380
He is.

210
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:55,913
With this development, there's
no doubt he's betrayed us.

211
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,320
I see.

212
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,620
Well, I can't say I'm shocked.

213
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:10,466
But that's some gratitude
after I took him in.

214
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:14,131
I treated that punk like a
brother, and this is what I get?

215
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,740
A pity, huh?

216
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Indeed it is.

217
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:21,245
He made it to the
manufacturing room, you said?

218
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,760
Here's what I'd do if I were him.

219
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,320
I'd destroy everything in sight.

220
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,120
Then I'd kidnap Caesar, I think.

221
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:45,730
Scratch that.

222
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,440
Maybe just kill him.

223
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:49,950
Bastard!

224
00:12:50,033 --> 00:12:51,657
How could you do this to my love?

225
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:53,916
Get him out of the way and it's over.

226
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:56,900
He's the only one who can make S .A .D.

227
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,680
Or rather, he's the only
one who even knows how.

228
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:06,240
Frankly, if Law is able to pull that off,

229
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:09,640
Then we've got a big problem, Brook.

230
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:16,340
To be specific, it's a problem for
me, because this is my business.

231
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:19,120
If it dries up, people will be angry.

232
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:22,397
Hey, Baby Five, what the hell
do you think you're doing?

233
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,917
You're lucky the young
master's so forgiving.

234
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,157
I'm gonna kill him with my own two hands.

235
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:29,120
You can't stop me, damn it!

236
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:30,653
This is the last straw!

237
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:34,500
They say misfortune never comes alone. Oh.

238
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:40,640
Oh, so my misfortune is
going to be his next.

239
00:13:42,020 --> 00:13:44,580
Poor Law, that adorable little scamp.

240
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:48,020
Young master, whatever are
you going to do to him?

241
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:52,420
You know darn well Law will
get exactly what he deserves.

242
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,620
That traitor.

243
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:58,880
I know this will be difficult for you,
Vergo, but I need you to take care of Law.

244
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,860
Also, make it as cruel and
gruesome as you can manage.

245
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,960
I want him to suffer.

246
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,680
I won't hold back.

247
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:12,237
In fact, Dolfi, I'll even take a
picture of this corpse for you.

248
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,261
How's that, son?

249
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:17,093
You remember my camera I'm always using?

250
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:18,062
That should do.

251
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,097
What the hell are you talking about?

252
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:21,592
You don't have a camera.

253
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:22,750
Oh, right.

254
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,337
Actually, I don't think I've ever
taken a single photo in my life.

255
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:28,773
How about I'll bring you an ear instead?

256
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:31,600
I like that idea even better.

257
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:33,742
Ba-da-ba-da-ba.

258
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,720
Aziza, Monet, can you hear me?

259
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,360
Joker, why, hello.

260
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:39,820
Oh, hello there.

261
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:44,160
You have to be careful with Law,
but Straw Hat's dangerous, too.

262
